{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-8","id":"msg_01UL7RtoFwEVtM6ULLrxriWM","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Anchor is a single-user productivity + R&D control system. Grounded summary:\n\n- **Purpose.** Anchor is a personal productivity system for J.C. Liechty that organizes tasks, projects, and ideas across life domains (academic, commercial, family, writing) using plain-text **markdown files as the single source of truth** â€” no database, everything in one folder (`C:\\dev\\Anchor`).\n\n- **What it ships â€” the app.** Its one declared deliverable is `anchor_gui.py`: a self-contained, **stdlib-only Python HTTP server** that renders an interactive browser dashboard at `http://localhost:8777`. It runs persistently as a Windows NSSM service (`anchor`), reads/writes the markdown files directly, and supports checking off tasks, adding tasks, capturing ideas, and full task lifecycle (active â†’ done â†’ cancelled / saved-for-later â†’ restored).\n\n- **CLI mirror.** `anchor.py` provides the same logic as command-line operations and generates a static `dashboard.html`.\n\n- **Self-testing.** `anchor_healthcheck.py` runs daily at 5 AM via Task Scheduler â€” it parses every file, boots a throwaway server, exercises every endpoint, and writes a dated report; failures surface as a red banner in the dashboard.\n\n- **Beyond task-tracking â€” the R&D \"Project Cockpit.\"** The larger build effort turns each project's window into a **mission-control cockpit for the \"trio\" workflow** (researchPrime â†’ Crucible â†’ Foreman). Each lane (Research Â· Planning Â· Build) shows its most-recent session as a **tile with one status light** (green=working, amber=needs-you, red=crashed, grey=idle/done); clicking expands an **inline panel** with a cached summary on top and a **real resizable terminal below**.\n\n- **The terminal substrate.** Sessions run as **persistent, server-side ConPTY terminals** (`pty_manager.py` â†’ `terminal_session.py` â†’ xterm.js over a hand-rolled WebSocket), each isolated in its **own git worktree**. Opening a session feels like a normal Claude/Gemini session â€” the lane's skill **auto-loads once and greets once** (no repeating-prompt loop). This is the one place Anchor waives its stdlib-only rule, via the optional `pywinpty` dependency.\n\n- **Supporting R&D modules** add: a session model and cached/validated summaries (`sessions.py`, `summarizer.py`), an effort/cost-tokens-time ledger (`effort_history.py`), deliverable declare/pin/launch-by-type (`deliverables.py`), brownfield discovery of on-disk artifacts, stage handoffs between planâ†’build, ephemeral deliverable previews (hard-guarded to never bind port 8777), and Ghost World Labs branding.\n\n- **Status.** This has shipped through **four R&D surface versions** (v2 \"sessions/summaries/grass,\" v3 \"Mission Control,\" v4 \"Project Cockpit\"); v4 was built by Foreman (9 waves green, 637 tests passing) and merged to master on 2026-06-13.\n\nBottom line: Anchor is both a **markdown-backed personal task dashboard** and, increasingly, a **local control surface for running and tracking AI \"trio\" R&D sessions** â€” all stdlib-Python, single-folder, no external dependencies except the optional terminal extra."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4418,"cache_read_input_tokens":45311,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4418,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":2,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a33874e3-7ea0-4777-9198-15ed0407ad52","uuid":"a276c0e2-bd4d-4b89-9932-912fa7306106","request_id":"req_011Cc1JUUpmPeXXKkhB6X2XU"}
